                <pb facs="0718" n="706" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg706"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.248/128: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-26T21:00:00-05:00">March 26, 1941—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>112. Your 163, March 24, 6 p.m. The Department has the matter of airplanes for
                    Greece under urgent consideration and it is hoped that a solution satisfactory
                    to Greece will be reached in the near future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
